SUMMARY:Native species seed collection (Chapel Hill)
DESCRIPTION:There are many ways to help restore native ecosystems. One easy way is to collect seeds of native plant species from one location and plant them in another. Join NCWF Tri-County Conservationists Chapter as they collect spicebush and other native seeds in Brumley Preserve. \nUsing the seeds we collect\, TCC will spread the seeds in areas needing these plants and they will grow seedlings to then plant in new rewilding oases in the preserve. Join us for a fun walkabout in Brumley Preserve while learning about native plant species and their seeds. Help strengthen our native ecosystems by spreading native seeds! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/native-species-seed-collection-chapel-hill/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
